5. Suspended VisionOS Dock (Floating Glassmorphism)
Instead of pinning an opaque navigation bar to the bottom edge of the screen, we made it a suspended pill floating 16px above the display edge:

Optical Translucency: backdrop-filter: blur(28px) saturate(200%) magnifies the colors passing behind it while turning harsh edges into smooth milk-glass reflections.

Physical Rim Bevel: An inner top rim highlight (inset 0 1px 1px rgba(255,255,255,0.22)) creates the illusion that the dock is a polished slab of molded sapphire crystal.

Micro-Haptics on Action: Buttons use active:scale-[0.98] and active:translate-y-[2px] paired with inner shadow activation, so every tap provides tactile feedback.

Summary Recipe for this Design Language
If you want to replicate this in other views or future projects, use this 5-point formula:

Never use #000000 flat: Use tiered dark slates (#0A0A0C → #16161A → #22222B).

Always add a top 1px inset specular highlight (rgba(255,255,255, 0.12 - 0.2)).

Split shadows into two: One for close contact occlusion, one for ambient floating diffusion.

Pair carved concave elements (trenches, inputs) with convex floating elements (cards, badges).

Use directional 165° gradients instead of solid matte colors to reflect ambient directional lighting.

