Apple Human Interface Design System: Light & Dark Theme GuideTo achieve the exact look and feel of the reference UI, you need to combine six foundational design pillars:Canvas Elevation Contrast (cool off-white canvas vs. pure white cards).Apple Electric Blue Pills (#007AFF with colored glow and high pill radius).Milled Segmented Controls (recessed track holding an elevated floating pill).Left-Accent Visual Anchors (the iconic blue vertical alert strip).Breathing Status Wells (mini-cards with soft glowing status LEDs).SF Pro Typography & Squircles (Apple-standard border radii and font weights).1. The Design Tokens (CSS Variables)The biggest secret to Apple's light mode is that the background is never pure white. The background is a soft, tinted slate-blue (#EEF2F6), which allows pure white cards (#FFFFFF) to visually elevate without heavy drop shadows.:root,
[data-theme="light"] {
  /* 1. Canvas & Slabs */
  --base-canvas: #EEF2F8;            /* Cool muted slate-blue background */
  --card-bg: #FFFFFF;                /* Pure white elevated cards */
  --card-border: rgba(226, 232, 240, 0.85); /* Hairline crisp boundary */
  
  /* 2. Recessed Trenches (Segmented track & input wells) */
  --trench-bg: #E4E9F2;              /* Recessed track background */
  --trench-active: #FFFFFF;          /* Floating active segment */
  --trench-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.08), 0 1px 2px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.04);

  /* 3. Apple Accent System */
  --apple-blue: #007AFF;             /* Primary iOS action blue */
  --apple-blue-hover: #0066D6;       /* Pressed state */
  --apple-blue-glow: 0 4px 14px rgba(0, 122, 255, 0.35); /* Soft colored shadow */
  --apple-green: #34C759;            /* Success / Active */
  --apple-amber: #F59E0B;            /* Warning / Busy */
  --apple-red: #FF3B30;              /* Critical */

  /* 4. Typography Ink */
  --ink-primary: #111827;            /* Deep obsidian text */
  --ink-secondary: #475569;          /* Subtitles & body */
  --ink-muted: #64748B;              /* Meta & inactive labels */
  --ink-subtle: #94A3B8;             /* Micro tags / placeholders */

  /* 5. Layered Diffuse Shadows */
  --shadow-card: 0 8px 24px -4px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.05), 0 2px 6px -1px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.03);
  --shadow-hover: 0 14px 30px -4px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.10);
}

[data-theme="dark"] {
  /* 1. Canvas & Slabs (True Obsidian OLED) */
  --base-canvas: #0B0C10;            /* Deep OLED Obsidian */
  --card-bg: #15171E;                /* Elevated dark titanium slab */
  --card-border: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.07); /* Specular top catch-light */

  /* 2. Recessed Trenches */
  --trench-bg: #1C1F28;              /* Milled dark groove */
  --trench-active: #282C37;          /* Elevated active pill */
  --trench-shadow: 0 3px 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);

  /* 3. Apple Accent System */
  --apple-blue: #0A84FF;             /* Apple Dark Mode Azure */
  --apple-blue-hover: #0071E3;
  --apple-blue-glow: 0 4px 16px rgba(10, 132, 255, 0.40);
  --apple-green: #30D158;
  --apple-amber: #FF9F0A;
  --apple-red: #FF453A;

  /* 4. Typography Ink */
  --ink-primary: #FFFFFF;
  --ink-secondary: #CBD5E1;
  --ink-muted: #94A3B8;
  --ink-subtle: #64748B;

  /* 5. Shadows */
  --shadow-card: 0 10px 28px -6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7), 0 2px 6px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
  --shadow-hover: 0 16px 36px -6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.85);
}
2. Anatomical Component BreakdownA. The "Pass" Button (Electric Blue Pill)Notice the reference button: it is completely rounded (border-radius: 9999px), has high contrast white text, and casts a colored shadow matching the button itself (not a gray shadow)..btn-apple-pass {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--apple-blue), var(--apple-blue-hover));
  color: #FFFFFF;
  border: none;
  border-radius: 9999px; /* Complete pill */
  padding: 8px 18px;
  font-size: 13px;
  font-weight: 700;
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 7px;
  cursor: pointer;
  box-shadow: var(--apple-blue-glow); /* Blue tinted glow shadow */
  transition: all 0.2s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
  user-select: none;
}

.btn-apple-pass:hover {
  transform: translateY(-1px);
  box-shadow: 0 6px 18px rgba(0, 122, 255, 0.45);
}

.btn-apple-pass:active {
  transform: translateY(0);
}
B. The Segmented Control Track (All Feed | Notices | Carpool | Neighbors)The segmented control sits inside a carved, recessed track with inner padding (5px). The active button is physically elevated with a discrete drop shadow./* Outer Track */
.ref-segmented-track {
  background: var(--trench-bg);
  border-radius: 20px;
  padding: 5px;
  display: flex;
  gap: 4px;
  user-select: none;
}

/* Individual Segment Tab */
.ref-tab-btn {
  flex: 1;
  border: none;
  background: transparent;
  padding: 10px 14px;
  border-radius: 15px;
  font-size: 13.5px;
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--ink-muted);
  cursor: pointer;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  gap: 6px;
  transition: all 0.2s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
}

.ref-tab-btn:hover {
  color: var(--ink-secondary);
}

/* Elevated Active Pill */
.ref-tab-btn.active {
  background: var(--trench-active);
  color: var(--ink-primary);
  font-weight: 700;
  box-shadow: var(--trench-shadow);
}
C. The Alert Card with Blue Accent Strip (RWA ALERT)The card has a continuous vertical accent line hugging its left edge. This is achieved cleanly using a ::before pseudo-element:.alert-accent-card {
  background: var(--card-bg);
  border-radius: 24px;
  border: 1px solid var(--card-border);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
  position: relative;
  overflow: hidden;
  padding: 18px 20px 18px 22px;
}

/* 5px Left-Border Highlight */
.alert-accent-card::before {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  left: 0;
  top: 0;
  bottom: 0;
  width: 5px;
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--apple-blue), #38BDF8);
  border-radius: 6px 0 0 6px;
}
D. The 3-Column Status Mini-Cards (Club Pool, Badminton, EV Charging)These cards use a responsive 3-column grid (display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr)), generous border radius (22px), and an LED indicator with an animated glow:.mini-status-card {
  background: var(--card-bg);
  border: 1px solid var(--card-border);
  border-radius: 22px;
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
  padding: 14px 10px;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  text-align: center;
  transition: transform 0.18s ease, box-shadow 0.18s ease;
}

.mini-status-card:hover {
  transform: translateY(-2px);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-hover);
}

/* LED Status Indicator */
.status-dot-glow {
  width: 10px;
  height: 10px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  margin-bottom: 7px;
}

.status-dot-glow.green {
  background-color: var(--apple-green);
  box-shadow: 0 0 10px var(--apple-green);
}

.status-dot-glow.amber {
  background-color: var(--apple-amber);
  box-shadow: 0 0 10px var(--apple-amber);
}
E. The Capsule Composer / Search BarThe search input is shaped like an elongated medicine capsule (border-radius: 26px), with a circular icon and a circular plus button on the right:.search-capsule-bar {
  background: var(--card-bg);
  border: 1px solid var(--card-border);
  border-radius: 26px;
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
  padding: 8px 10px 8px 16px;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 12px;
}

.search-plus-btn {
  width: 32px;
  height: 32px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background: rgba(0, 122, 255, 0.12); /* Subtle blue tint */
  color: var(--apple-blue);
  border: none;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  cursor: pointer;
  font-weight: 800;
  font-size: 16px;
  transition: background 0.15s ease;
}

.search-plus-btn:hover {
  background: rgba(0, 122, 255, 0.22);
}
